# PRE20-ALIGN Product Readiness Scorecard

| Dimension | Score | Status | Rationale |
|---|---:|---|---|
| Frontend productization | 38/100 | Engineering surface | User management works, but most pages are read-only, actionless, or expose internal C-label semantics. |
| Backend alignment | 64/100 | Partially aligned platform | Gates, tenant checks, persistence, and APIs exist, but execution is metadata/mock-only and many capabilities are not product-bound. |
| DB consistency | 76/100 | Mostly tenant-shaped | Most business and observability tables have org_id; remaining drift is concentrated in permission assignments, callback transitions, global identity/session/security state, and static registries. |
| Overall alignment | 59/100 | Internal platform | Backend and DB are ahead of the product UI; full feature chains are incomplete. |

## What The System Can Do Now

| Capability | Current Real State |
|---|---|
| User management | UI can create, edit, disable, enable, reset password, and manage permissions. |
| Read operational data | UI can list jobs, artifacts, reviews, errors, operation logs, modules, agents, and workflows. |
| Dashboard health | UI can show backend health, operation log projections, approval counts, module readiness, permission status, and live gate readiness. |
| Tenant persistence | Core jobs/artifacts/reviews/approvals/memory/operation/C17/C15/PRE20 ops records are mostly org_id scoped. |
| Execution gating | Backend can evaluate execution requests through C05/C12/C13/C14/C18/C09/C10 controls. |
| Callback/DLQ persistence | Backend can persist callback, result, DLQ, callback_state, and dlq_state records. |

## What The System Cannot Do From UI

| Missing Product Workflow | Blocking Layer |
|---|---|
| Create/switch organizations | Frontend/proxy |
| Manage org members | Frontend/proxy |
| Manage API keys | All layers |
| Trigger module execution | Frontend/proxy/runtime |
| Approve/reject approvals | Frontend/proxy |
| Create jobs/artifacts/reviews/errors | Frontend/proxy |
| Submit review decisions | Frontend/proxy |
| Edit live gate policy, canary, rollback | Frontend/proxy |
| Operate C15 callback/DLQ/replay | Frontend/proxy |
| Operate C17 anomaly/replay | Frontend/proxy/product API |
| Manage module/agent/workflow registries | Frontend/proxy |

## Hidden Backend Capabilities

| Hidden Capability | Why It Is Not Productized |
|---|---|
| Org and membership management | No UI/proxy binding |
| Module binding and sharing | No UI/proxy binding |
| Approval write workflow | Dashboard is read-only |
| Module adapter action request | UI disabled and proxy POST missing |
| Live gate writes | GET-only UI/proxy |
| C15 callback/failure/DLQ/replay | No product workflow |
| C17 anomaly/replay/audit storage | No product workflow |
| Registry writes | Product pages are read-only |
| C14 dependency/binding management | Control-plane/engineering-only |

## Engineering-Only Exposure

| Exposure | Product Risk |
|---|---|
| C17/C18/C12/C15/C05/PRE20-Q labels | Users see implementation milestones instead of product concepts |
| Adapter contract/provider metadata | Users see integration internals rather than actions |
| Mock/no-execution/read-only badges | Product appears unfinished or intentionally disabled |
| System Operations Control Center copy | Dashboard frames the app as a control plane |
| Capability registry language | Navigation and pages describe architecture rather than user outcomes |

## Final Classification

| Question | Answer |
|---|---|
| Is the system truly a product? | No |
| Is it still an engineering platform? | Yes |
| Main blocker | Product workflows do not close across UI -> API -> backend runtime -> DB for orgs, execution, approvals, live operations, C15 recovery, API keys, and record creation. |
| Best next phase | PRE20-PRODUCT FINAL should focus on productizing complete feature chains, hiding internal C-labels, and deciding the remaining DB tenant-shape gaps before adding new capabilities. |

